       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="KVS Class 1 Admission List 2026 – Check Selection Status">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title">KVS Class 1 Admission List 2026-27: Your Guide to Checking Selection Status</h1>
                    <p>The much-anticipated Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan (KVS) Class 1 admissions for the academic year 2026-27 are in full swing! For countless parents across India, securing a spot in a Kendriya Vidyalaya is a dream come true, promising quality education and a holistic development environment. If you've applied for your child's admission to Class 1, the crucial moment of checking the selection list is fast approaching. This comprehensive guide will walk you through everything you need to know about the KVS Class 1 Admission List 2026, including how to check the selection status, important dates, eligibility, and the transparent lottery system.</p>

                    <div class="highlight-text">
                        "The KVS Class 1 admission process for 2026-27 is conducted entirely online, emphasizing a fair and transparent computerized lottery system for selection."
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">KVS Class 1 Admissions 2026-27: Key Dates at a Glance</h2>
                    <p>The Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan has released a clear schedule for the Class 1 admissions. Keeping track of these dates is vital to ensure you don't miss any critical steps, especially the declaration of the provisional lists.</p>

                    <table>
                      <thead>
                        <tr>
                          <th>Event</th>
                          <th>Date</th>
                        </tr>
                      </thead>
                      <tbody>
                        <tr>
                          <td>KVS Admission Notice Release</td>
                          <td>March 19, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Online Registration for Class 1 Begins</td>
                          <td>March 20, 2026 (10:00 AM)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Last Date to Submit Online Application for Class 1</td>
                          <td>April 2, 2026 (11:59 PM)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>First Provisional List for Class 1 &amp; Balvatika</td>
                          <td>April 9, 2026 (Class 1) / April 8, 2026 (Balvatika)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Second Provisional List (if seats remain vacant)</td>
                          <td>April 16, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Third Provisional List (if seats remain vacant)</td>
                          <td>April 21, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                      </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Check KVS Class 1 Selection Status 2026</h2>
                    <p>Once the provisional lists are released, parents can check their child's admission status through the official KVS admission portal and individual school websites. Here's a step-by-step guide:</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official KVS Admission Portal</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the official Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan admission portal: <a href="https://kvsonlineadmission.kvs.gov.in" target="_blank">kvsonlineadmission.kvs.gov.in</a> or <a href="https://admission.kvs.gov.in" target="_blank">admission.kvs.gov.in</a>.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Provisional List Link</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for a prominent link related to "Lottery Result for Class 1 Admissions 2026" or "Provisional Selection List for Class 1".</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Login Credentials</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a login page where you need to enter your unique Login Code/Registration Number, your child's date of birth, and the registered mobile number.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. View Admission Result</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Click on the "Login" or "Submit" button. The KVS Class 1 Admission 2026 result will be displayed on your screen, indicating whether your child has been selected or is on the waitlist.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">5. Check Individual School Websites</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Many Kendriya Vidyalayas also publish their provisional lists on their respective official websites. You can find links to individual KV school websites through the KVS portal's directory.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Eligibility Criteria for KVS Class 1 Admission 2026</h2>
                    <p>Before applying, it's crucial to ensure your child meets the eligibility requirements set by KVS for Class 1 admissions.</p>

                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Age Limit:</strong> The child must be a minimum of 6 years old and a maximum of 8 years old as of March 31, 2026.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Age Relaxation:</strong> A relaxation of two years in the maximum age limit is applicable for differently-abled children.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Birthdate Consideration:</strong> Children born on April 1st are also considered eligible.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Nationality:</strong> Indian citizens and children of Foreign Nationals residing in India are eligible.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">The KVS Lottery System: Fair and Transparent</h2>
                    <p>KVS Class 1 admissions are conducted through a fair and transparent computerized lottery system, eliminating the need for any written exams or interviews for the younger classes. This system prioritizes admissions based on several categories:</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Right to Education (RTE) Quota</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">25% of the seats are reserved under the RTE Act for children residing within the vicinity of the school, with complete fee exemption.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Differently-Abled Children</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">After the RTE quota, children with special needs are given preference.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Service Priority Categories</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">The remaining seats are filled based on a priority system for children of central government employees, armed forces personnel, state government employees, and other categories.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Reservation for SC, ST, OBC, EWS</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Specific percentages of seats are reserved for Scheduled Castes (15%), Scheduled Tribes (7.5%), Other Backward Classes - Non-Creamy Layer (27%), and Economically Weaker Sections (EWS).</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Documents Required for Admission</h2>
                    <p>Once your child is selected, you will need to submit several documents for verification at the allotted Kendriya Vidyalaya. It is advisable to have these ready in advance.</p>

                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Child's Birth Certificate</p>
                        <p>✅ Recent Passport-size Photograph of the child</p>
                        <p>✅ Proof of Residence (e.g., Aadhaar, Ration Card, Electricity Bill)</p>
                        <p>✅ Caste Certificate (for SC/ST/OBC categories, if applicable)</p>
                        <p>✅ Service Certificate (for Central/State Government employees, if applicable)</p>
                        <p>✅ EWS/BPL Certificate (if applicable)</p>
                        <p>✅ Aadhaar Card details of the child and parents</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">What Happens After the KVS Admission List is Released?</h2>
                    <p>If your child's name appears on the provisional selection list, congratulations! The next steps are crucial to confirm their admission.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Document Verification</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You must visit the allotted Kendriya Vidyalaya with all the original required documents for verification. Failure to provide accurate and complete documents can lead to the cancellation of admission.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Fee Payment</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">After successful document verification, you will need to pay the prescribed admission fees to confirm your child's seat.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Waiting List and Subsequent Lists</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">If your child is on the waiting list, there's still hope! KVS will release second and third provisional lists if seats remain vacant after the initial rounds of admissions. Keep an eye on the official portal for these updates.</div>
                    </div>

                    <p>The KVS Class 1 admission process is designed to be streamlined and transparent. By staying informed about the dates, eligibility criteria, and checking the selection lists promptly, you can navigate this important phase successfully. We wish all aspiring students the very best for their KVS Class 1 admissions for the 2026-27 academic session!</p>
                </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
